  "verbalization": "Armodafinil is implicated in the pathogenesis of Narcolepsy through a series of indirect pathways, primarily via Modafinil, which is a known indication for Narcolepsy. The evidence suggests that Armodafinil may act as a precursor or mediator in the development of Narcolepsy, as it is associated with X-linked Adrenoleukodystrophy and Balo Concentric Sclerosis, both of which have Modafinil as an indication and Narcolepsy as a downstream condition. This implies a potential role for Armodafinil in the broader pathophysiology of Narcolepsy, possibly through mechanisms involving neuroinflammation or metabolic pathways. The shared indication of Modafinil with Narcolepsy across multiple paths highlights a possible functional link between Armodafinil and Narcolepsy, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence supports a hypothesis that Armodafinil may contribute to Narcolepsy through a chain of indications that involve Modafinil, suggesting a possible ontological relationship that warrants further investigation.",
